  "body": "Closes #505\n\nCompletes the C-SDLC v3 authority transition. Merging this PR is the operator-approved atomic cutover: the tracked generation selector becomes canonical on `main`, while feature branches remain on v2 until their selector matches canonical `origin/main`.\n\nThe final implementation uses one shared authority contract across v2 dispatch and v3 local, remote, terminal, and install routes; removes repository-writable approval fallbacks; uses an advisory lock in the Git common directory; preserves durable rollback from a fresh linked worktree; and keeps focused proof execution credential-sanitized, repository-bounded, and fail-closed.\n\nC-SDLC v2 remains authoritative before merge. Terminal reconciliation records the completed transition after merge; it is not a second activation gate. V2 retirement remains separate post-cutover work.\n\nRequired before merge: a passing independent exact-head review and green required hosted checks.",
